gm-method (editor viewport black = kit opaque bg behind WebGL canvas; CDN cache lags publish): editor viewport renders BLACK because the kit app shell paints opaque var(--bg) on body/.app BEHIND the alpha WebGL canvas -- gameplay hides it by drawing opaque pixels, the editor does not. Fix: kit canvas-host modifier class on body + local always-served override in client/style.css (body.canvas-host, body.canvas-host .app { background: none !important }). NEVER chase the camera for 'editor black' -- check the shell background first. CRITICAL: relying ONLY on the kit CSS from a CDN is FRAGILE because CDN cache lags a publish (rule observed absent even after publishing). Always own a local copy of critical kit overrides served from your own assets, belt-and-suspenders with the CDN version.